sections.text:
Mixing units is the most frequent error. Convert milliwatts to watts, or hertz to kilohertz, before substituting. Adding powers in watts and gains in decibels without converting is another common fault.

Other mistakes are:
confusing bandwidth with data rate;
forgetting noise when calculating a link budget;
using the wrong logarithm base for decibels;
assuming a formula applies outside its conditions;
treating software output as correct because it looks precise;
ignoring the assumptions in a traffic or propagation model.

Also state your assumptions clearly. An examiner needs to see how you reached the answer, not only the final number.
